    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d384">

                <pb facs="0604" n="502" sameAs="frus:frus1935v01/pg502"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">504.418B1/173</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Director General of the Pan American Union</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Rowe</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1935-04-15">April 15, 1935</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: The Seventh
                    International Conference of American States, held at Montevideo in 1933, adopted
                    a resolution in which the Governments of the States of America were urged to
                    sign <pb facs="0605" n="503" xml:id="pg503"/> the Roerich Pact<anchor n="3"
                        xml:id="d384-f1"/> for the protection of artistic and cultural institutions
                    and historic monuments.</p>
                <p>In compliance with the resolution of the Conference, the Governing Board of the
                    Pan American Union at a session held on April 4, 1934, formulated the
                    fundamental principles of the Roerich Pact in the form of an inter-American
                    treaty, and at a session held on February 6, 1935, it adopted a recommendation
                    of the Committee of the Board on the Roerich Pact and opened the treaty to the
                    signature or adherence of all the States of the world. This treaty is deposited
                    with the Pan American Union and is opened on this date, April 15, 1935, to the
                    signature or adherence of all the States.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to send to you herewith a certified copy of the above mentioned
                    treaty, together with copies of the antecedents<anchor n="4" xml:id="d384-f2"/>
                    to which reference has been made.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>L. S. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Rowe</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d384-f1" n="3" xml:id="d384-f1-content">
                <p>Proposed by Nicholas K. Roerich, founder and former honorary president of the
                    Master Institute of United Arts, New York City.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d384-f2" n="4" xml:id="d384-f2-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
